# E321 draft: repairing the OHOS SDK lld host runtime without changing target linking

id:                     E321
trigger_tool:           conan|cmake|clang|lld|ctest
phase:                  configuration|linking|testing|runtime
error_signature:        Process not started.*\[permission denied\]|[0-9]+% tests failed.*BAD_COMMAND|The active OHOS SDK linker failed its GNU-flavor probe

severity:               3
category:               ohos-sdk|linking|testing|elf-execution
match_keywords:         lld -flavor gnu, GNU ld fallback, BAD_COMMAND, permission denied, libxml2.so.16, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, CTest
title:                  OHOS SDK lld host-runtime repair must preserve target linker semantics

root_cause:             Repairing the OHOS SDK lld host runtime has two independent scope hazards. A bare invocation of the generic lld driver can return nonzero because no linker flavor was selected, falsely activating a GNU ld fallback. That fallback bypasses the configured SDK clang/lld path and can produce target test executables rejected by HarmonyOS execution policy. Separately, keeping the SDK host LD_LIBRARY_PATH active during CTest leaks host-only libraries into target process startup and makes otherwise valid tests report BAD_COMMAND.
affected_scope:         OHOS Conan/CMake builds that repair the SDK lld libxml2.so.16 dependency and then execute generated target binaries on a HarmonyOS worker or device.
verification_cmd:       LD_LIBRARY_PATH="${SDK_LLVM_LIB}:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:-}" "${SDK_LLVM_LIB%/lib}/bin/lld" -flavor gnu --version && ctest --output-on-failure --no-tests=error

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           preserve-sdk-lld-with-scoped-host-runtime
rec_description:        Derive llvm/lib from the active Conan compiler, require its ABI-matched libxml2.so.16, probe the generic driver with -flavor gnu, and prepend that directory only while CMake configures, builds, or installs. Restore the environment before CTest and fail fast if the SDK linker remains unusable.
rec_command:            SDK_LLVM_LIB="$(dirname "$(dirname "$("$CXX" -print-resource-dir)")")"; LD_LIBRARY_PATH="${SDK_LLVM_LIB}:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:-}" "${SDK_LLVM_LIB%/lib}/bin/lld" -flavor gnu --version
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-environment

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      fail-fast-with-linker-stderr
fallback_description:   If the active SDK has no matching libxml2.so.16 or its flavor-aware lld probe fails, stop recipe generation with the probe stderr instead of silently changing linkers.
fallback_command:       conan create . --build=missing
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          conan-exception

forbid_1_pattern:       -fuse-ld=/data/service/hnp/bin/ld|CMAKE_(EXE|SHARED|MODULE)_LINKER_FLAGS.*fuse-ld
forbid_1_reason:        A system GNU ld fallback changes the target linker path after the SDK lld probe and bypasses the toolchain behavior expected by HarmonyOS CI.
forbid_1_consequence:   Compilation and linking may finish, but every generated test executable can fail to start with permission denied.
forbid_2_pattern:       LD_LIBRARY_PATH=.*llvm/lib.*(ctest|cmake\.test)|with.*build_environment.*cmake\.test
forbid_2_reason:        The SDK llvm/lib directory contains host linker runtime libraries and must not remain active while target executables run.
forbid_2_consequence:   CTest reports the complete suite as BAD_COMMAND even though configure and compilation succeeded.

principles:             P010, P014, P017

causes:                 []
caused_by:              [E120, E132]
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         [E266]
prerequisite_of:        []

